    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) is green, and the project compiled cleanly \u2014 which means the OpenAPI-generated DTOs and MapStruct mappers picked up the new fields without issue.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe request now accepts an optional `birthDate`, and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns a derived `ageBand` (`MINOR` <18, `ADULT` 18\u201364, `SENIOR` 65+) computed against `registrationDate`.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added behaviour as small, self-contained units rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **`util/AgeBands.java`** (new) \u2014 one tiny static `of(birthDate, asOf)` classifier, zero surrounding complexity.\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `birthDate` field with plain getter/setter plus a `@Transient getAgeBand()` that just delegates to `AgeBands`. Because the getter name matches the DTO property, MapStruct auto-maps it \u2014 so I did **not** touch the `OwnerMapper` expressions or any existing complex method.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 `birthDate` on `OwnerFields` (input) and read-only `ageBand` on `Owner` (output).\n4. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to all four `schema.sql` files, and fixed the one positional seed file (`db/hsqldb/data.sql`) that the tests actually load. The h2/postgres seeds use named-column inserts, so they needed no change.\n\nI deliberately avoided editing the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` and the `OwnerMapper` mapping block; the only Java functions I touched are the three trivial (CC=1) accessors on `Owner` and the new util method.\n\nOne note worth flagging: `db/mysql/data.sql` already had positional owner inserts inconsistent with its own schema (7 values against a wider table) before this change \u2014 a pre-existing issue unrelated to the age-band work, and it isn't exercised by the test profile (`hsqldb`).",
